{0 hermetic}

A standard library prelude that refuses ambient authority.

In a file that opens {!Hermetic}, a use of a standard library value that
reaches the world without being handed it is a type error. A source file
opens it on its first line:

{[
open! Hermetic
]}

{1:api API}

{!modules: Hermetic}

{!Hermetic} is the prelude: the standard library, [Unix] and [Thread], with
each refused value given a type nothing consumes and an alert that says why.
The [Hermetic__] units it aliases hold the restated modules; a program names
them through {!Hermetic}, never directly.
